  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U9U-READ-1",
      "title": "The Bus That Broke Down",
      "text": "Last Saturday our basketball team took a bus to a game in Taichung. On the highway, the old bus broke down. All the passengers got off and waited beside the road. Our coach called a mechanic, and he arrived in an hour. While we waited, we took a short break under a tree and shared two boxes of rice balls. A couple of players practiced shooting at an old basket near a store. Some of us were afraid the trip would break up, but the mechanic fixed the engine before noon. We got to the gym ten minutes before the game, and the school band was still on the stage. Our team won by two points, and the satisfaction was really big. That night, numerous fans left messages on our school website."
    }
  ],
